\f0\fs24 \cf0 I want you to write a data acquisition program in Matlab using the data acquisition toolbox for national instrument input/output boards.\
\
Please do this by writing code only in the folder that contains this file.  You do not need to access any other files.  I will test the code myself.  You only need to write and review it, doing your best to ensure that it will work.\
\
The code should build a GUI using inline code and use the modern data acquisition toolbox (not the legacy one).\
\
GUI should have the following components.\
1. A list box to choose the data acquisition board to use\
2. A \'93setup acquisition\'94 button that gets everything ready to trigger and run\
3. A \'93calibration\'94 button that links to a function that I will write later.  Please provide a hook\
4. A \'93start acquisition\'94 button that launches the acquisition.  This should read in 5 analog inputs at 1 kHz.  In addition, it should use one analog output to control laser power (0-5V) and a digital output (TTL) to open and close a shutter around the acquisition.  For every 100 ms of data, the program should call a \'93process\'94 function that I will write later that will return four scalars: lifetime, intensity, s and g.  The program should plot lifetime and intensity in real time in a chart recorder window showing a rolling user specified time of data.  The s and g should be plotted as a phasor plot on a unit half circle.  The data should be streamed to disk and not kept in memory after plotting and saving.\
5. An \'93end acquisition\'94 button that cleans up and prepares for the next acquisition.\
\
Please provide the following extra functionality:\
1. A way of saving, loading, and applying the acquisition settings \
2. A way for the user to specific extra analog and digital inputs to read in, potentially plot, and save.}